ment ids with non-overlapping time ranges as re-clones, the operator host's fsck reports no issues. The MCP server's own fsck (read through the MCP server, 2026-11-04 ~01:46 PST, after deploy of 4496e9acd2a) still reports env_id_mismatch: own env eea68b7f (its .env-id dates from 2026-08-26 PDT) against ad49f17f and b2b5c498, which nothing on the operator host identifies.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- The server's ranges genuinely overlap: blue-green deploys run two containers against one shared tickets clone, so two environments can write in the same window.\n- The overlap rule's display-name matching pairs different writers who share a name across the server's environments.\n- ad49f17f / b2b5c498 belong to another writer (e.g. the review-bot clone or CI bridge) whose events reach the server clone.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The two foreign environment ids are identified (which writer, which time range per author) from read-only evidence.\n- [ ] Either fsck stops reporting a benign case with a regression test, or the row is shown to be a real overlap and its message says what the operator should do.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_id":"c4d9-7807-5c55-4b93","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Server fsck still reports ENV_ID_MISMATCH after the overlap rule","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f3d02719-000e-41d2-a5ee-ecabe36d6b81","39377bc8-b435-4289-ad20-763e35109e94"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793794661965555878,"uuid":"d743ceb8-b0a3-405b-8ae3-a95167db28fc"}